0..76 Comment "//! A walk along a path that a data field holds. The family of the data type"
77..107 Comment "//! computes the field\'s type."
108..111 Comment "//!"
112..189 Comment "//! A family can return a path type as a code. A field at that family holds a"
190..265 Comment "//! path. The type of the path is the decode of the family\'s answer. A walk"
266..345 Comment "//! along such a path reads the path\'s endpoints off its type. So the type must"
346..386 Comment "//! read as the path type it decodes to."
387..390 Comment "//!"
391..466 Comment "//! Both checkers read the field\'s type at the type its family returns. The"
467..545 Comment "//! walk then transports along the path, as a walk along a path at its written"
546..560 Comment "//! type does."
561..564 Comment "//!"
565..581 Comment "//! - see: #5359"
582..661 Comment "//! - see: `model/identity/transport-list.gandr` — a walk along a path at its"
662..680 Comment "//!   written type"
682..746 Comment "/// A value of the first type with a value of the type it picks."
